Package: icloud-bridge
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Corbin Jurgens <corbinjurgens@gmail.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), cifs-utils, sudo, systemd, unison (>= 2.52)
Recommends: python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtsvg
Suggests: docker-ce | docker.io
Homepage: https://github.com/corbinjurgens/icloud-vm-for-linux
Description: iCloud Drive on Linux via a minimal Windows VM
 Bridges iCloud Drive to a Linux host by running Apple's official iCloud for
 Windows client inside a dockur/windows guest and re-exporting the sync root
 over SMB to /mnt/icloud.
 .
 This package installs the host side: the CIFS mount and automount units, the
 health-check timer, the privileged power helper that turns the whole bridge on
 and off as one transaction, the PySide6 tray application and status window, and
 the guest provisioning scripts under /usr/share/icloud-bridge.
 .
 Installing is not sufficient on its own. Everything machine-specific -- the
 share password, the mount ownership, and the sudo grant for the power helper --
 is applied by running "sudo icloud-bridge-configure --env-file /path/to/.env".
 .
 PySide6 is a Recommends rather than a Depends so the host half remains
 installable on systems whose archives lack the python3-pyside6 packages; the
 launcher reports the exact missing pieces if the GUI is started without them.
